  "description": "Heartbeat scheduling for micro-task parallel loops: sequential by default, each thread splitting off half of its remaining work for an idle worker at most once per heartbeat, so per-task overhead stays a bounded fraction of run time even for nanosecond-scale iterations. Allocation-free per loop.",
